Ddoc

$(D_S $(TITLE),

$(P
$(B dlang-dockerized) is a $(EM community project) that packages D compilers as OCI images.
These can be used with OCI-compliant container engines — such as
$(LINK2 https://docs.docker.com/engine/install/, Docker)
$(LINK2 https://podman.io/get-started, Podman) or
$(LINK2 https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/, Kubernetes).
)

$(NOTE
OCI stands for $(STRONG $(LINK2 https://opencontainers.org/, Open Container Initiative)).
)


$(H2 Quick Start)

$(H3 Docker)
$(CONSOLE docker run --init --rm -it -v .:/src ghcr.io/dlang-dockerized/dmd:latest dmd)

$(H3 Podman)
$(CONSOLE podman run --init --rm -it -v .:/src ghcr.io/dlang-dockerized/dmd:latest dmd)

$(H3 Common CLI flags)

$(P
The provided command runs the container image for $(CODE dmd) from $(CODE ghcr.io).
It mounts the current working directory $(CODE .) as volume $(LPAREN)$(ARG -v)$(RPAREN) under $(CODE /src) in the container.
)

$(P
$(ARG --rm) instructs the container engine to automatically remove the container
and any anonymous unnamed volume associated with the container when it exits.
)

$(P
$(ARG -it) is actually a combination of the flags $(ARG -i) and $(ARG)
and requests an interactive session — even if detached — with a pseudo-TTY.
)

$(P
Given that most applications are not designed to be run as PID $(CODE 1),
using $(ARG --init) the container engine can be instructed to inject a tiny $(EM init system)
which takes care of the $(EM signal handling) requirements for PID $(CODE 1) of the Linux kernel
as well as $(EM reaping orphaned zombie processes).
)

Further information can be found in the corresponding manuals:
$(UL
$(LI $(LINK https://docs.docker.com/reference/cli/docker/container/run/))
$(LI $(LINK https://docs.podman.io/en/latest/markdown/podman-run.1.html))
)


$(H2 Containerfiles)

$(UL
$(LI $(CODE $(NBSP)ghcr.io/dlang-dockerized/dmd))
$(LI $(CODE $(NBSP)ghcr.io/dlang-dockerized/ldc))
$(LI $(CODE docker.io/dlangdockerized/dmd))
$(LI $(CODE docker.io/dlangdockerized/ldc))
)

$(P
Container images are built from so-called $(EM Containerfile)s —
also known as $(EM Dockerfile)s when used with $(EM Docker).
)

$(P
These Containerfiles are compiled from templates and meta data.
)

$(P
A repository providing pre-rendered Containerfiles can be found at:
$(LINK https://github.com/dlang-dockerized/containerfiles)
)

$(P
The source template files as well as the template engine are located in the $(EM packaging) repository:
$(LINK https://github.com/dlang-dockerized/packaging)
)

$(P
Documentation for the format of Containerfiles can be found over there:
$(LINK https://github.com/podman-container-tools/container-libs/blob/main/common/docs/Containerfile.5.md)
)


$(H3 Packaged software)

$(UL
$(LI $(H4 DMD — Digital Mars D Compiler)
    $(UL
    $(LI DUB — official package manager for the D programming language)
    $(LI rdmd — rapid edit-run cycle companion)
    )
)
$(LI $(H4 LDC — LLVM-based D Compiler)
    $(UL
    $(LI DUB — official package manager for the D programming language)
    $(LI LLD — Linker of the LLVM project)
    $(LI LLDB — Debugger of the LLVM project)
    $(LI rdmd — rapid edit-run cycle companion)
    )
)
)

$(NOTE
Please note that not all software listed above is available across all image versions.
This applies to images providing legacy compiler versions in particular.
)


$(H3 Compiler versions)

$(P
$(I dlang-dockerized) aims to package the latest compilers as well as “relevant” legacy versions.
)

$(P
To select a specific version of a container image, append a version prefix to the image name.
)

$(NOTE
The prefix $(CODE latest) refers to the latest stable release of the corresponding image.
)

$(CONSOLE $(SHE) Containerfile

$(SHE) latest stable release
FROM ghcr.io/dlang-dockerized/dmd:latest

$(SHE) latest release of the 2.100.x branch (→ 2.100.2)
FROM ghcr.io/dlang-dockerized/dmd:2.100

$(SHE) 2.100.0 release
FROM ghcr.io/dlang-dockerized/dmd:2.100.0
)

$(P
Images are rebuilt from time to time in order to ship dependency updates and similar.
)

$(P
For legacy versions of the bundled software it may be necessary to apply
custom patches and/or backports in order prior to building.
These modifications can be found in the
$(LINK2 https://github.com/dlang-dockerized/packaging/tree/main/resources/patches, $(CODE patches) subfolder)
in the $(EM packaging) repository.
)


$(H3 Base images)

$(P
A base image is the start of all Containerfiles.
It serves as the base of the container and as such provides a runtime environment.
)

$(P
A common convention is to append a suffix to the tag of the container image
that consists of an alias referring to the base image.
)

$(UL
$(LI $(CODE ghcr.io/dlang-dockerized/dmd:$(EM baseimage)))
$(LI $(CODE ghcr.io/dlang-dockerized/dmd:latest-$(EM baseimage)))
$(LI $(CODE ghcr.io/dlang-dockerized/dmd:2-$(EM baseimage)))
$(LI $(CODE ghcr.io/dlang-dockerized/dmd:2.100.2-$(EM baseimage)))
$(LI $(SMALL and so on))
)


$(H3 Maintained versions and images)

$(P
The $(STRONG maintenance policy) of $(I dlang-dockerized) is outlined in the MAINTENANCE document of the project.
It can be found at $(LINK https://github.com/dlang-dockerized/packaging/blob/main/MAINTENANCE.md).
)

$(NOTE:
Keep in mind, this is work done by volunteers.
)


$(H2 Container registries)

Container images are pushed to two container registries:
$(UL
$(LI GitHub Container Registry: $(LINK https://github.com/orgs/dlang-dockerized/packages/container/package/dmd))
$(LI Docker Hub: $(LINK https://hub.docker.com/r/dlangdockerized/dmd/tags))
)

The registry to pull an image from is selected
by prepending the corresponding registry host and vendor name to the image name:
$(UL
$(LI GitHub Container Registry: $(CODE $(EM ghcr.io/dlang-dockerized/)dmd))
$(LI Docker Hub: $(CODE $(EM docker.io/dlangdockerized/)dmd))
)

$(NOTE
At the time of writing, $(STRONG $(EM ghcr.io)) is the $(STRONG recommended registry) to pull these images from.
)

$(NOTE
$(EM Docker) defaults to $(CODE docker.io);
allowing users to omit that prefix.
$(BR)
Best practice is, however, to explicitly specify the source registry of an image.
This ensures compatibility across container engines and user configurations.
)


$(H2 Tips and tricks)

$(H3 Debugging with LLDB)

$(P
At the time of writing, due to a limitation in LLDB,
$(EM seccomp confinement) needs to be turned off for the debugger to work.
$(CONSOLE docker run --security-opt seccomp=unconfined -it dlang-dockerized/ldc:latest lldb /src/my-app)
)

$(P
For further information check out: $(LINK https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/61899)
)


$(H2 Issue tracker)

See: $(LINK https://github.com/dlang-dockerized/packaging/issues)


$(H2 Packaging your own app as container image)

$(P
The following examples outline how one can build and package their own application using OCI containers.
They are meant to be used as a starting point only.
Downstream users are expected to adjust them accordingly to fit their requirements and tune them to their liking.
)

$(NOTE
The D community is usually more than happy to help you with getting your Containerfile set up and running.
)


$(H3 No build system)

$(OL
$(LI Navigate into the root folder of your project.)
$(LI Create a file named $(CODE Dockerfile) $(LPAREN)no file extension$(RPAREN) in that directory.)
$(LI Copy and paste the following template:
$(CONSOLE $(SHE) build stage
FROM ghcr.io/dlang-dockerized/dmd:latest AS build-stage
COPY . /d-project
RUN dmd -inline -O -i -I=/d-project/src /d-project/src/app.d -of=/my-d-app

$(SHE) runtime stage
FROM docker.io/debian:latest
COPY --from=build-stage /my-d-app /usr/local/bin/my-d-app
CMD ["/usr/local/bin/my-d-app"]
)
)
$(LI Adjust as needed.)
$(LI Run $(ICODE docker build . --tag my-d-app:v1.0.0) to build the container image.)
)


$(H3 Using DUB)
$(OL
$(LI Navigate into the folder of your project
    where your $(I DUB recipe) $(LPAREN)i.e. $(CODE dub.json) or $(CODE dub.sdl)$(RPAREN) is located.)
$(LI Specify a $(CODE targetPath) and a $(CODE targetName) in your DUB recipe.
$(SMALL While this step is optional,
it will make it easier to copy the right binary into the runtime stage later.)
)
$(LI Create a file named $(CODE Dockerfile) $(LPAREN)no file extension$(RPAREN) in that directory.)
$(LI Copy and paste the following template:
$(CONSOLE $(SHE) build stage
FROM ghcr.io/dlang-dockerized/dmd:latest AS build-stage
COPY . /d-project
RUN dub build --build=plain

$(SHE) runtime stage
FROM docker.io/debian:latest
COPY --from=build-stage /targetPath/targetName /usr/local/bin/my-d-app
CMD ["/usr/local/bin/my-d-app"]
)
)
$(LI Adjust as needed.)
$(LI Run $(ICODE docker build . --tag my-d-app:v1.0.0) to build the container image.)
)

)


Macros:
    TITLE=Docker and OCI images

    ARG=$(TC code, arg, $0)
    CODE=$(T code, $0)
    CONSOLE=$(PRE $(CODE $1))
    ICODE=$(T code, $(T b, $1))
    SHE=#
